  "kanji": "都",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 都\ntitle: metropolis\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 11\nradical: 邑\nradicalNumber: 163\nonyomi: [ト, ツ]\nkunyomi: [みやこ]\ndistractors: [部, 院, 者]\n---\n\n# 都 — metropolis\n\n**Strokes:** 11 · **Key (radical):** 邑 (as right-hand 阝, no. 163) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n都 appears in words for cities and capitals. [都会](../words/都会.md) とかい describes a city or urban setting,\nwhile the native word 都 みやこ can mean a capital or seat of government.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** see 者 beside the right-hand 阝 and imagine people gathered in a metropolis.\nThis is a learning image, not a historical explanation.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe table selects useful readings; the metadata preserves the complete source reading list.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ト | on | [都会](../words/都会.md) とかい — city; 京都 きょうと — Kyoto |\n| みやこ | kun | 都 みやこ — capital |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [都会](../words/都会.md) とかい — city; urban setting\n- 都 みやこ — capital\n- 京都 きょうと — Kyoto\n\n## Notes\n\nLearn 京都 as きょうと; the 都 there is ト.\n[都会](../words/都会.md) does not imply that the city is a national capital.\n[部](部.md) shares the right-hand 邑 form 阝 but replaces 者 with a different left-hand cluster.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\nDictionary: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1444950, 1444970, 1652350.\n",
